ing Income into quartiles to handle high skewness in income levels.\n# Usefulness: Simplifies income into discrete ranges for capturing broader patterns of financial capacity.\ndf[Income_Binned] = pd.qcut(df[Income], q=4, labels=[Low, Medium, High, Very High])', '# Employed_x_YearsEmployed\n# Interaction feature multiplying Employed by YearsEmployed to highlight stability for currently employed applicants.\n# Usefulness: Measures the compound effect of being employed and years of experience, making it relevant for stability assessment.\ndf[Employed_x_YearsEmployed] = df[Employed] * df[YearsEmployed]', '# Married_x_Age\n# Interaction feature combining Age and Married status to reflect stability with life stage.\n# Usefulness: Captures the potential advantages of maturity and marital stability during credit evaluation.\ndf[Married_x_Age] = df[Married] * df[Age]', '# One-hot encoding for Industry\n# Converts Industry into multiple binary columns for each sector.\n# Usefulness: Allows the model to capture sector-specific patterns that may influence financial behavior.\ndf = pd.get_dummies(df, columns=[Industry], prefix=Industry, drop_first=True)', '# One-hot encoding for Ethnicity\n# Converts Ethnicity into multiple binary columns for each group.\n# Usefulness: Captures socioeconomic differences across ethnic groups that may influence credit behavior.\ndf = pd.get_dummies(df, columns=[Ethnicity], prefix=Ethnicity, drop_first=True)', '# Target Encoding for Industry\n# Encodes Industry by the mean success rate of each category.\n# Usefulness: Provides aggregated success information by job sector while retaining variability per group.\nindustry_te = df.groupby(Industry)[Target].transform(mean)\ndf[Industry_TargetEncoded] = industry_te', '# Removing unnecessary columns\n# Drops ZipCode because it lacks meaningful predictive value for credit success.\ndf.drop(columns=[ZipCode], inplace=True)']
